.TH MUSIKITE 1 "2026-11-24" "MusiKitE" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
musikite \- music practice for wind instruments and piano (Python package musikite)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B musikite
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B musikite
.RI [ command ]
.B \-\-help
.br
.B python3 \-m musikite
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B MusiKitE
is an exerciser for wind instruments, bands and piano: reading and playing (graded from the
microphone or a MIDI keyboard), drills, ear training, an exercise library, routines and a
practice diary. Its Python package is
.BR musikite ;
.B musikite
is made by
.I ./install.sh
(pip, in the conda base); without installing, the script
.I bin/musikite
of the project does the same. Both run
.B python3 \-m musikite
from any folder. The old name
.B python3 \-m musictools
still works.
.PP
Without a window it makes duets, canons and second voices, reads vector PDFs into MIDI,
merges MIDI files and writes trumpet fingerings into PDFs. With a window it opens the app
.RB ( gui )
or a staff viewer
.RB ( view ).
.PP
MIDI files are always at concert pitch; scores and PDFs are engraved at written pitch.
Chords and keys of duets and canons are given at written trumpet pitch unless
.B \-\-concert
is used.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B gui
The main window of MusiKitE.
.TP
.BI view " file.mid|file.pdf"
Staff viewer with a moving cursor.
.B \-\-page
wrapped systems instead of one line;
.BI \-\-bpm " BPM"
tempo for Play;
.BI \-\-instrument " NAME"
for a PDF whose instrument is not written in it.
Click a bar: Play starts there after one count-in bar; double-click: it starts at once.
.TP
.BI play " file.mid"
Play a MIDI file in real time (FluidSynth). Give the soundfont with
.BR \-\-sf2 .
.TP
.B duet
Random duet for two Bb trumpets.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-c " CHORDS" "\fR, \fP\-\-chords"
progression, one chord per bar; \(lqF:G\(rq = two chords in a bar
(default \(lqC F G G C F G C\(rq).
.TP
.BI \-g " N" "\fR, \fP\-\-rounds"
times the progression is repeated (2).
.TP
.BI \-l " 1|2|3" "\fR, \fP\-\-level"
complexity (1).
.TP
.BI \-k " KEY" "\fR, \fP\-\-key"
e.g. C or Am (default: the first chord).
.TP
.B \-\-concert
chords and key at concert pitch.
.TP
.BI \-s " SEED" "\fR, \fP\-\-seed"
random seed: the same seed gives the same duet.
.TP
.BI \-t " BPM" "\fR, \fP\-\-bpm"
tempo (120).
.TP
.BI \-f " N" "\fR, \fP\-\-phrase"
bars per phrase, the last one is the cadence (4).
.TP
.BI \-x " LIST" "\fR, \fP\-\-textures"
comma-separated textures: thirds, sixths, melody_acc, pedal, dialogue, echo, canon_bar
(level 1), canon_half, mirror, counterpoint (level 2).
.TP
.BI \-r " X" "\fR, \fP\-\-repetition"
0..1, how much the motif is restated (0.7).
.RE
.TP
.B canon
Canon for two Bb trumpets: trumpet 2 plays what trumpet 1 played one progression earlier.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-c " CHORDS"
progression (\(lqC F G C\(rq).
.TP
.BI \-d " 1-5"
difficulty: 1 = one long note per chord ... 5 = eighths (2).
.TP
.BI \-b " N"
beats per chord (4).
.TP
.BI \-n " N"
cycles of the progression (4).
.TP
.BR \-k " KEY, " \-\-concert ", " \-s " SEED, " \-t " BPM"
as in
.B duet
(tempo 80).
.RE
.TP
.BI second_voice " melody.mid"
Duet from a melody: the melody of the MIDI (the track with the most notes, or
.BI \-\-track " N"\fR,\fP
0 = the first) plus a second voice for
.BI \-\-instrument " KEY"
(a catalogue key, e.g. \(lqC (trombone)\(rq; default: the current instrument).
.RS
.TP
.BI \-m " MODE"
.B harmony
(same rhythm, a third or a sixth away),
.B canon
(the melody delayed) or
.B accompaniment
(notes of the chords; default).
.TP
.BR \-\-side " below|above, " \-\-interval " thirds|sixths"
harmony.
.TP
.BR \-\-delay " auto|\(lqhalf bar\(rq|\(lq1 bar\(rq|\(lq2 bars\(rq|\(lq4 bars\(rq, " \-\-canon_interval ", " \-\-strict ", " \-\-allow_dissonant
canon (refused under 70 % consonance unless
.BR \-\-allow_dissonant ).
.TP
.BR \-\-pattern " auto|\(lqlong notes\(rq|\(lqhalf notes\(rq|beats|arpeggio"
accompaniment (arpeggio).
.RE
.TP
.BI pdf " score.pdf"
MIDI from a vector PDF (MuseScore, Sibelius, Finale, Dorico, MusiKitE).
.BI \-\-instrument " NAME"
if it is not written in the PDF;
.B \-\-force
writes the MIDI even if some bars do not add up.
.TP
.BI merge " a.mid b.mid ..."
All the tracks of the files in one MIDI (\-o for the output). Files with different tempo
maps are refused unless
.BR \-\-allow_tempo_mismatch .
.TP
.BI fingering " part.pdf"
A copy of a trumpet part with the Bb trumpet fingerings under the notes, default
.IR part.noted.pdf .
.BI \-o " out.pdf"\fR,\fP
.BI \-\-fontsize " PT"
(12),
.BI \-\-font " FILE"
(TTF/OTF for the digits),
.BI \-\-space " PT"
(12),
.B \-\-color " r|g|b|k"
(k),
.B \-\-no_repetition
(repeated pairs written once, then \(lq\-\(rq),
.BI \-\-instrument " trumpet"\fR.\fP
.TP
.B check
Dependency check: what is installed, what is missing and the commands to install it.
Exit status 1 if something required is missing.
.SH COMMON OPTIONS
For
.BR duet ", " canon ", " second_voice ", " pdf ", " merge ", " play :
.TP
.BI \-o " out.mid" "\fR, \fP\-\-out"
write the result to a MIDI file.
.TP
.BI \-\-pdf " out.pdf"
engrave the result to a PDF.
.TP
.BI \-\-sf2 " font.sf2"
soundfont used to play.
.TP
.B \-\-play
play the result.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I install.sh
installation from the source code (asks before every step;
.B \-\-yes
answers yes to all,
.B \-\-help
lists the steps).
.TP
.I bin/musikite
the command without installing; add to
.I ~/.zshrc
the line
.B export PATH="<project folder>/bin:$PATH"
(with it,
.B man musikite
finds this page in
.IR <project>/man ).
.TP
.I ~/.musikite/
users, settings, results, diary (or the data folder chosen in Settings > Folders);
.IR log.txt ,
.IR scoreread.log .
.TP
.I ~/musikite/
default folders of workspaces, exercises, MIDI, PDF, scores, audio, results, soundfonts.
.TP
.I musikite/data/
soundfont GeneralUser GS, fonts, icon, exercise library.
.TP
.I docs/
the full manual (also Help > Manual in the app).
.SH REQUIREMENTS
Python 3.10 or later with the packages of
.IR requirements.txt ;
FluidSynth and PortAudio 19.7 or later. Run
.B musikite check
on a new computer.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
musikite duet \-c "C F G C" \-l 2 \-s 7 \-o duet.mid \-\-pdf duet.pdf
musikite canon \-d 3 \-k Bb \-o canon.mid
musikite second_voice melody.mid \-m harmony \-o duet.mid
musikite pdf part.pdf \-o part.mid
musikite merge a.mid b.mid \-o all.mid
musikite fingering part.pdf
musikite view part.pdf \-\-page
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR docs/command-line.md ,
.I docs/README.md
(the manual).
